1
00:05:49,411 --> 00:05:55,411
Where Is Anne Frank is a animation, drama, family film directed by Ari Folman.

2
00:11:38,823 --> 00:11:44,823
The film follows the journey of Kitty, the imaginary
friend to whom Anne Frank dedicated her diary.

3
00:17:28,235 --> 00:17:34,235
A fiery teenager, Kitty wakes up in the near future in Anne Frank's house in Amsterdam and
embarks on a journey to find Anne, who she believes is still alive, in today's Europe.

4
00:23:17,647 --> 00:23:23,647
While the young girl is shocked by the modern world,
she also comes across Anne's legacy.

5
00:29:07,058 --> 00:29:13,058
Anne Frank (voice), played by Emily Carey.

6
00:34:56,470 --> 00:35:02,470
Kitty (voice), played by Ruby Stokes.

7
00:40:45,882 --> 00:40:51,882
Anne's Peter (voice), played by Sebastian Croft.

8
00:46:35,294 --> 00:46:41,294
Kitty's Peter (voice), played by Ralph Prosser.

9
00:52:24,705 --> 00:52:30,705
Otto Frank (voice), played by Michael Maloney.

10
00:58:14,117 --> 00:58:20,117
Edith Frank (voice), played by Samantha Spiro.

11
01:04:03,529 --> 01:04:09,529
Where Is Anne Frank is a 2021 animated magic realism film
directed by Israeli director Ari Folman.

12
01:09:52,941 --> 01:09:58,941
The film follows Kitty, Anne Frank's imaginary friend to whom she
addressed her diary, manifesting in contemporary Amsterdam.

13
01:15:42,352 --> 01:15:48,352
Seeking to learn what happened to her creator, Kitty attracts worldwide
attention and interacts with undocumented immigrants.

14
01:21:31,764 --> 01:21:37,764
Where Is Anne Frank was shown out of competition at the
2021 Cannes Film Festival on 9 July 2021.

15
01:27:21,176 --> 01:27:27,176
It was released in France on 8 December 2021 by Le Pacte, on 15 December 2021 in Belgium by
Cinéart, on 16 March 2022 in Luxembourg, and on 30 March 2022 in the Netherlands.

16
01:33:10,588 --> 01:33:16,588
The tone is emotional.
